      "rule": "A milestone cannot be released without the required real frontend and public-entry black-box evidence for the changed user path.",
      "evidence": "The task note explicitly records that real Rex LLM consumption and frontend status refresh still require validation on the changed candidate. The plan requires real Rex frontend observation and public-entry evidence for notification failure labeling, worker snapshot behavior, status projection, foreground-owner changes, and waiting_user precedence. The supplied author evidence contains isolated Rex CLI probes and focused/unit tests, but no evidence for the required post-change frontend/status-refresh path.",
      "remediation": "Run and record the required changed-candidate black-box acceptance through the real Rex frontend and the public Collab entry points. Cover one complete notification submission path, Rex worker snapshot through the public request, Rex rejection labeling, and status transitions for idle, working, waiting_user, stale owner, done, error, and unknown state. Keep the existing isolated probe evidence as lower-layer evidence; do not use it as a substitute."
